{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA (2026-08-17): CONFIRMED dynamic root cause. `src/rebar/grounding/harness.py:254-267` hard-codes `multiprocessing.get_context(\"fork\")` on every POSIX host; `run_in_worker` reaches it at lines 310-316 and calls `Process.start()`. With one live background thread, runtime tracing observed CPython 3.12 execute `multiprocessing/popen_fork.py:66 -> os.fork()` and emit `DeprecationWarning: This process ... is multi-threaded, use of fork() may lead to deadlocks in the child`. Direct `os.fork()` and direct fork-context Process probes produced the identical warning; a spawn-context probe returned the expected value without warning, ruling out xdist, payload behavior, and generic process creation as causes. The original focused xdist subset passed 47 tests under warning-as-error, so xdist is not a deterministic prerequisite. Compatibility experiment: running the 47-test lifecycle matrix under spawn preserved 46/47 behaviors; only the reap-lag test failed because its fixture mutates the Process with a local unpicklable closure before start. Forkserver was rejected as a drop-in because its Unix-domain control socket conflicts with the unit network guard and the same fixture is unpicklable. Caller sweep found no production caller in-repo, but `run_in_worker` is publicly re-exported at `src/rebar/grounding/__init__.py:40,94`; its current POSIX fork semantics execute arbitrary closures/lambdas, whereas spawn requires picklable/importable callables. Thus the caller-dependency gate requires an explicit callable contract before repair. Recommended contract: fork only in single-threaded hosts; spawn in multithreaded hosts; convert start/pickling failures to the existing fail-open RunResult rather than propagate. Phase 2 remains locked pending behavior approval."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787017564054662001,"uuid":"e69f5a7f-72e3-4a87-8a1d-275e1b0852fc"}